# ESP-IDF component selection for the ESP32-S3 BSP.
#
# The ESP-IDF package (packages/ESP-IDF-latest) ships a SConscript that only
# knows the ESP32-C3 (and, in newer forks, C6) file sets; for the S3 target it
# raises NameError because no branch defines its source list. Rather than
# patching the vendored package, the BSP declares its own esp-idf group here.
#
# The lists below are the **ESP-IDF v6.1** esp32c3_* sets taken from the package
# SConscript (curated for v6.1 by the C3/C6 port), with every `esp32c3` path
# rewritten to its existing `esp32s3` counterpart.  v6.1 renamed the whole
# peripheral layer (hal/* -> esp_hal_*, driver/* -> esp_driver_*, newlib ->
# esp_libc), so this list differs substantially from the ESP-IDF v5.1 one it
# replaces.  Every entry is checked to exist in the package tree.
#
# Deliberate differences on top of the C3 set:
#   - Wi-Fi / BT / wpa / lwip / netif / vfs / nvs / esp_phy / esp_event groups:
#     not compiled (console-only BSP, matching the BSP's Kconfig defaults)
#   - components/cxx, esp_pm, app_update, efuse, pthread: kept exactly as C3 so
#     IDF startup code sees the same symbol set (unused pieces drop out via
#     --gc-sections)
#   - RISC-V arch files (components/riscv/*, esp_system/port/arch/riscv) replaced
#     by their esp_system/port/arch/xtensa counterparts plus the target-
#     independent components/xtensa interrupt plumbing, and linked against
#     xtensa/esp32s3/libxt_hal.a (xthal_save_extra_nw / window spill / cp regs)
#   - No esp32s3 counterpart exists in v6.1 for esp_hw_support adc2_init_cal.c
#     (S3 has no ADC2), so it is dropped.
#   - lowpower/port/esp32s3/sleep_cpu.c dropped, same reason as the ESP32-C3
#     package list: its only possible caller is sleep_modes.c, reached under
#     CONFIG_PM_POWER_DOWN_CPU_IN_LIGHT_SLEEP && SOC_PM_CPU_RETENTION_BY_RTCCNTL
#     (both true on S3). RT-Thread owns the idle path and this BSP compiles only
#     pm_trace/pm_locks/pm_impl out of esp_pm, so that config is kept off (see
#     sdkconfig_s3.h) and nothing references the file. It is also not
#     compilable with the config off: esp_sleep_tagmem_pd_low_init()'s #else
#     branch assigns through s_tag_mem, which the #if above it does not define.
#     (An upstream v6.1 bug: esp32c3/sleep_cpu.c has no such #else branch.)
#   - Added because the S3 has capabilities the C3 lacks:
#       * esp_hal_security/mpu_hal.c   - S3 has MPU regions, C3 has none
#       * esp_hal_gpio/esp32s3/rtc_io_periph.c - per-target RTC IO table
#       * spi_flash/spi_flash_wrap.c    - SOC_CACHE_SUPPORT_WRAP=1 on S3 and
#         cache_utils.c calls spi_flash_wrap_probe()/spi_flash_wrap_enable()
#       * esp_rom/patches/esp_rom_cache_writeback_esp32s3.S - the S2/S3 cache
#         ROM shim (esp_rom_cache_esp32s2_esp32s3.c) calls
#         cache_writeback_items_freeze(), which only exists in that .S
#       * esp_hal_touch_sens/touch_sens_hal.c - SOC_TOUCH_SENSOR_SUPPORTED=1 on
#         S3 (0 on C3), so sleep_modes.c's touch_wakeup_prepare() calls
#         touch_hal_prepare_deep_sleep()
#   - Left out of the xtensa arch set deliberately: esp_ipc_isr* (dual-core IPI,
#     CONFIG_ESP_SYSTEM_SINGLE_CORE_MODE makes esp_ipc.c call handlers
#     directly) and expression_with_stack* (indexes the real FreeRTOS TCB, which
#     the RT-Thread wrapper does not provide).
#   - bootloader_sha / secure_boot / flash_encrypt are left out: they need
#     mbedtls (psa/crypto.h) and secure boot, both off for this BSP.  Nothing
#     in this build references bootloader_sha256_* either - its only caller,
#     bootloader_utility.c, is not part of the set - so the weak fallbacks in
#     ../idf_port/src/rt-thread_balance_stub.c are all that is ever needed.
#   - esp_hw_support/sleep_modes.c IS built (C3 builds it too, and the
#     per-SoC rtc_sleep.c calls into it).  What it is *not* allowed to pull in
#     is the CPU-retention path, so CONFIG_PM_POWER_DOWN_CPU_IN_LIGHT_SLEEP is
#     kept off - see sdkconfig_s3.h; that also keeps
#     lowpower/port/esp32s3/sleep_cpu.c out of the set.
#   - mbedtls sources are not built, so esp_crt_bundle.c (needs mbedtls/pk.h)
#     and esp_crypto_shared_gdma.c (only reachable from mbedtls aes/sha GDMA)
#     are dropped as well.

import os
